cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the schema, the MCP designs, the privacy contract, or the
  reporting-app flows in your own work, please cite this archive.
type: software
title: "AZ One Health Sentinel — a participatory-surveillance stack for Arizona"
abstract: >-
  A working knowledge framework for participatory One Health surveillance
  in Arizona, built across EpiHack Arizona 2026. The stack pairs a
  mobile-first anonymous reporting app (Next.js + React + TypeScript)
  with an eight-agent FastAPI backend, eleven FastMCP servers wrapping
  vector-borne-disease and heat data sources, and a DuckLake-on-Postgres
  knowledge graph (572 nodes / 791 edges / 1027 properties) covering
  all 15 Arizona counties, 22 tribal nations, 16 pathogens, historical
  outbreaks, and the standards crosswalk (SNOMED / ICD-10 / LOINC).
  Frozen for archival 2026-05.
